  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="bg-white py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22]">
          Lock Rekeying Questions — Answered
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
            What is the difference between rekeying and replacing a lock?
            <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Rekeying changes the internal pin configuration of an existing lock cylinder so that only a new key works — the lock hardware itself stays in place. Lock replacement involves removing the entire lock and installing brand-new hardware. Rekeying is significantly less expensive and achieves the same security result when the lock hardware itself is in good condition. Lock replacement is the better choice when the existing hardware is damaged, worn, low quality, or you want to upgrade to a higher-security lock.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
            Will my old keys definitely not work after rekeying?
            <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Yes — 100%. When a lock is rekeyed, the internal pins are physically replaced with a new set configured to a different key cut pattern. The old key's profile no longer matches the new pin heights, so it cannot operate the lock. Every old key — including any copies that were made — is immediately and permanently deactivated. Only the new keys we cut to the rekeyed pattern will work.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
            Can you rekey my locks if I don't have a working key?
            <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Yes. If you don't have a working key, we first need to pick or bypass the lock to open it, and then rekey the cylinder. This adds a small amount of time to the service but is a very common scenario — particularly after a lockout, a lost key situation, or when someone moves into a home where no working key was provided. We handle this regularly throughout Delaware.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
            Can you rekey my locks so they all use one key?
            <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Yes — this is called "keyed alike" service and it is one of the most popular rekeying requests we receive. We rekey every lock in your home to the same pin configuration so one key operates all of them. This works even if your existing locks are different brands or models. The result is a clean, convenient setup where one house key opens your front door, back door, side door, and any other entry points you have included.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
            How many locks can you rekey in one visit?
            <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            We can rekey as many locks as you need in a single visit. Most homes have two to four exterior lock cylinders, which we can complete in well under an hour. Larger properties or rental units with more entry points take a bit longer but are still typically handled in one efficient visit. Let us know how many locks you have when you call and we can give you a realistic time estimate.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
            What brands of locks can you rekey?
            <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            We rekey all major residential lock brands including Kwikset, Schlage, Defiant, Baldwin, Yale, and others. If you have a high-security lock such as Medeco, Mul-T-Lock, or Abloy, these can also be rekeyed — call us and we will confirm based on the specific model. The only locks that cannot be rekeyed are certain very cheap or proprietary lock designs, but these are uncommon in standard residential properties throughout Delaware.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 group">
          <summary class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] text-lg cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center">
            Do you serve all of Kent County for lock rekeying?
            <span class="text-[#A61E22] text-2xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Yes — we serve the entire Kent County area including <a href="/service-areas/dover-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Dover</a>, <a href="/service-areas/milford-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Milford</a>, <a href="/service-areas/smyrna-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Smyrna</a>, <a href="/service-areas/camden-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Camden</a>, <a href="/service-areas/harrington-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Harrington</a>, <a href="/service-areas/frederica-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Frederica</a>, <a href="/service-areas/felton-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Felton</a>, <a href="/service-areas/magnolia-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Magnolia</a>, <a href="/service-areas/woodside-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Woodside</a>, <a href="/service-areas/wyoming-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Wyoming</a>, <a href="/service-areas/cheswold-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Cheswold</a>, <a href="/service-areas/clayton-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Clayton</a>, <a href="/service-areas/leipsic-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Leipsic</a>, <a href="/service-areas/little-creek-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Little Creek</a>, <a href="/service-areas/bowers-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Bowers</a>, <a href="/service-areas/viola-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Viola</a>, <a href="/service-areas/kenton-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Kenton</a>, <a href="/service-areas/hartly-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">Hartly</a>, and all surrounding communities. Call (302) 735-0050 to schedule your rekeying service anywhere in Delaware.
